    {
      "id": "90407e30ccd93823735b5386ec1f8113e65298a7",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1566755082,
          "type": null,
          "body": "From doc/README.developer\n\nWhen printing or displaying the values of 64-bit integral data types,\n\ndon't use \"%lld\", \"%llu\", \"%llx\", or \"%llo\" - not all platforms\n\nsupport \"%ll\" for printing 64-bit integral data types.  Instead use\n\nthe macros in <inttypes.h>, for example:\n\n\nThe build breakages from the Z21 dissector were not using unsupported specifiers, it was having values that were wider than the specifier.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
